!Added from donor mechanism
!---------------------------------------------------------------------------
! **************************************************   Diethyl carbonate reactions   ************************************************
!                                 ******************************************************************
!                                                  *** Initiation: Diethyl carbonate ***
!                                 ******************************************************************
! HN = Hisashi Nakamura
! WJP = William J. Pitz
!------------------------------------------------------
!*** Molecular elimination from diethyl carbonate   ***
!------------------------------------------------------
!Ea, A from Rate expression diethyl carbonate(Manion et al JPCA 101, 1997
!DEC=C2H4+CCOC*OOH    1.1E13 0.0 4.63E4
!ref: C.M. Grégoire et al., CNF (2023) 112594. R4
! from all experiments; p = 1.5 bar; Sela et al. Proc. Combust. Inst. 38 (2021), 987-996
DEC=CCOC*OOH+C2H4    4.365E13 0.0 4.8815E4
!---------------------------------------------------------
!*** Unimolecular decomposition of diethyl carbonate   ***
!---------------------------------------------------------
!From Sarathy et al, C8, C_F (2011)
CJCOC*OOCC+H=DEC    1.0E14 0.0 0.0E0
!From Sarathy et al, C8, C_F (2011)
CCJOC*OOCC+H=DEC    1.0E14 0.0 0.0E0
!From Sarathy et al, C8, C_F (2011)
CCOC*OOCJ+CH3=DEC    1.0E13 0.0 0.0E0
!Assumed the same as high pressure rate forch3o+ch3=)ch3och3 from Fischer et al., Dimethyl Ether, IJCK 3 2:713?E40 (2000).
!CCOC*OOJ+C2H5=DEC    3.0E13 0.0 0.0E0
!ref: C.M. Grégoire et al., CNF (2023) 112594. R18
!COOPER MODIFICATION was 3.0E13 Assumed the same as high pressure rate forch3o+ch3=)ch3och3 from Fischer et al., Dimethyl Ether, IJCK 3 2:713   740 (2000). Recent Measurement of DME decomp by Cook et al and as
CCOC*OOJ+C2H5=DEC    1.63E12 0.0 5.846E4
!Assumed the same as high pressure rate forch3o+ch3=)ch3och3 from Fischer et al., Dimethyl Ether, IJCK 3 2:713?E40 (2000).
!CCOCJ*O+C2H5O=DEC    3.0E13 0.0 0.0E0
!ref: C.M. Grégoire et al., CNF (2023) 112594. R19
!COOPER MODIFICATION was 3.0E13 Assumed the same as high pressure rate forch3o+ch3=)ch3och3 from Fischer et al., Dimethyl Ether, IJCK 3 2:713   740 (2000).
CCOCJ*O+C2H5O=DEC    1.63E12 0.0 5.846E4
!-------------------------------------------
!*** o2 additions to diethyl carbonate   ***
!-------------------------------------------
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F (2011) degeneracy=6
DEC+O2=CJCOC*OOCC+HO2    6.6E13 0.0 5.23E4
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al, C8 C_F (2011) degeneracy=4
DEC+O2=CCJOC*OOCC+HO2    4.4E13 0.0 4.82E4
!--------------------------------------
!***   DEC H-atom Abstraction rxns  ***
!--------------------------------------
!HNv4.1e taken from Mendes et al. JPCA 118 (2014) 4889-4899, degeneracy=6, factor=2.5, EE beta
DEC+OH=CJCOC*OOCC+H2O    3.41E1 3.62 -2.73E2
!HNv4.1e taken from Mendes et al. JPCA 118 (2014) 4889-4899, degeneracy=4, factor=2.5, EE alpha
DEC+OH=CCJOC*OOCC+H2O    1.34E1 3.66 -4.095E3
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=6
!DEC+H=CJCOC*OOCC+H2    1.33E6 2.54 6.756E3
!ref: C.M. Grégoire et al., CNF (2023) 112594. R10
!the average value taken from Wang et al. Chem. Phys. Lett. 2014(616) 109-114, primary beta, degeneracy=6
DEC+H=CJCOC*OOCC+H2    1.154E11 1.206 9.895E3
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=4
!DEC+H=CCJOC*OOCC+H2    2.41E6 2.4 2.583E3
!ref: C.M. Grégoire et al., CNF (2023) 112594. R11
!the average value taken from Wang et al. Chem. Phys. Lett. 2014(616) 109-114, secondary alpha, degeneracy=4
DEC+H=CCJOC*OOCC+H2    3.168E10 1.234 6.084E3
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=6
DEC+CH3=CJCOC*OOCC+CH4    9.06E-1 3.65 7.154E3
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=4
DEC+CH3=CCJOC*OOCC+CH4    2.4E-9 6.36 8.93E2
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=6
DEC+O=CJCOC*OOCC+OH    1.96E6 2.43 4.75E3
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=4
DEC+O=CCJOC*OOCC+OH    1.53E6 2.41 1.14E3
!HNv4.1e taken from Mendes et al. JPCA 117 (2013) 14006-14018, degeneracy=6, factor=2.5, primary beta
DEC+HO2=CJCOC*OOCC+H2O2    2.06E0 3.98 1.87149E4
!HNv4.1e taken from Mendes et al. JPCA 117 (2013) 14006-14018, degeneracy=4, factor=2.5, secondary alpha
DEC+HO2=CCJOC*OOCC+H2O2    1.89E-4 4.9 1.0684E4
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=6
DEC+CH3O=CJCOC*OOCC+CH3OH    4.34E11 0.0 6.458E3
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=4
DEC+CH3O=CCJOC*OOCC+CH3OH    9.16E5 0.0 2.873E3
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=6
DEC+CH3O2=CJCOC*OOCC+CH3O2H    1.39E0 3.97 1.828E4
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=4
DEC+CH3O2=CCJOC*OOCC+CH3O2H    4.12E2 3.12 1.319E4
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=6
DEC+C2H3=CJCOC*OOCC+C2H4    1.0E12 0.0 1.8E4
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=4
DEC+C2H3=CCJOC*OOCC+C2H4    8.0E11 0.0 1.43E4
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=6
DEC+C2H5=CJCOC*OOCC+C2H6    1.0E11 0.0 1.34E4
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=4
DEC+C2H5=CCJOC*OOCC+C2H6    4.0E11 0.0 7.9E3
!------------------------------------
!***  radical H addition to DEC   ***
!------------------------------------
!Analogy with ch2o+h=ch2oh, Held and Dryer, IJCK, 30, 805 (1998)
DEC+H=>CCOC*OOH+C2H5    3.79E16 -1.39 5.402E3
!------------------------------------------
!***  consumption of radicals from DEC  ***
!------------------------------------------
!WJP: Analogy with ch2o+hco from Dooley et al. IJCK2010 (They base Ea on Radom's Ea for ch3 addition to ch2o)
CH2O+CCOCJ*O=CCOC*OOCJ    3.89E11 0.0 2.2E4
!WJP: isomerization to ccjoc*ooc and decomposition (to avoid adding a new species ccjoc*ooc)
CCOC*OOCJ=CH3CHO+CH3OCO    9.1E0 2.55 1.096E4
! rate constant is analogous to primary to secondary isomerization rate in alkanes. Sarathy et al. CnF2011
!HN Analogy with c2h5o+c2h4 [K. Yasunaga, et al., J. Phys. Chem. A 114 (2010) 9098-9109]
CJCOC*OOCC=CCOC*OOJ+C2H4    2.28E11 0.667 2.35E4
!Analogy with reaction rate rule ch3ch2ch2c*o+ch2o=ch3ch2ch2c*oocj from Huynh and Violi JOC 2008.
CCOCJ*O+CH3CHO=CCJOC*OOCC    1.11E1 3.14 1.12E4
!Analogy with rate of pc4h9o(=)c4h8oh-3. from Zheng and Truhlar 2008
CCOC*OOJ=CCJOC*OOH    5.32E-10 6.2 6.71E3
!Analogy with rate of pc4h9o(=)c4h8oh-4. from Sarathy about Butanol isomers mech_ver 4.5
CCOC*OOJ=CJCOC*OOH    1.32E-1 3.63 2.69E3
!Analogy with rate of ch3o+ccc=c=o(=)cccjc*ooc from Huynh and violi (3a=3h+ch3o) JOC 2008
C2H5O+CO2=CCOC*OOJ    5.58E1 2.81 5.97E3
!REF: PRIVATE COMMUNICATION FROM S.J. KLIPPENSTEIN, 2013 (Analogy with rate of ch3oco=ch3o+co):
CCOCJ*O=C2H5O+CO    8.691E17 -1.81 1.36567E4
    PLOG/5.0E-2 1.03E3 1.29E0 2.5401E4/
    PLOG/1.0E0 4.09E5 8.1E-1 2.19691E4/
    PLOG/1.0E1 9.02E14 -1.72E0 2.17675E4/
    PLOG/1.0E2 2.825E22 -3.44E0 2.35924E4/
!REF: PRIVATE COMMUNICATION FROM S.J. KLIPPENSTEIN, 2013 (Analogy with rate of ch3oco=ch3+co2):
CCOCJ*O=C2H5+CO2    8.691E17 -1.81 1.36567E4
    PLOG/5.0E-2 9.72E12 -1.31E0 9.4167E3/
    PLOG/1.0E0 1.25E16 -1.83E0 1.13408E4/
    PLOG/1.0E1 1.04E18 -2.1E0 1.28269E4/
    PLOG/1.0E2 8.69E17 -1.81E0 1.36567E4/
