HOC*OOH+H=>CO2+OH+H2    3.14E-21 3.14 8.7E3
!from C4 ver 53.6 (wu et al., J. Phys. Chem. A 2007, 111, 6693-6703).A-factor X 2 for 2 OH groups
HOC*OOH+O=>CO2+2OH    2.92E-3 4.73 1.73E3
!Assume rate  for c2h5oh+ch3 from C4 ver 53.6. A-factor X 2 for 2 OH groups
HOC*OOH+CH3=>CO2+OH+CH4    4.07E0 3.57 7.72E3
!--------------------------------------------------
!*** Unimolecular decomposition of C*COC*OOCC   ***
!--------------------------------------------------
!C*COC*OOCC = C2H4 + C*COC*OOH      5.5E+12 0.00 4.63E+04  !Analogy with rate of dec = c2h4 + ccoc*ooh from current work.
!                                                        Reduce A-factor by 2 for degeneracy
!Analogy with rate of dec = c2h4 + ccoc*ooh from current work.
C*COC*OOCC=C2H4+C*COC*OOH    7.9E12 0.0 4.65E4
!                                                        Reduce A-factor by 2 for degeneracy
!Analogy with rate of ccoc*ooh =) c2h5oh + co2 from current work.
C*COC*OOH=>CH3CHO+CO2    1.24E13 0.0 3.27E4
!------------------------------------
!*** O2 additions to C*COC*OOCC   ***
!------------------------------------
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al, C8 C_F (2011) deneracy=2
C*COC*OOCC+O2=C*COC*OOCJC+HO2    2.2E13 0.0 4.82E4
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F (2011) deneracy=3
C*COC*OOCC+O2=C*COC*OOCCJ+HO2    3.3E13 0.0 5.23E4
!----------------------------------------------
!***   c*coc*oocc H-atom Abstraction rxns   ***
!----------------------------------------------
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011) degeneracy=3
C*COC*OOCC+OH=C*COC*OOCCJ+H2O    5.28E9 0.97 1.586E3
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F (2011)
C*COC*OOCC+OH=C*COC*OOCJC+H2O    1.15E11 0.51 6.3E1
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011)degeneracy=3
C*COC*OOCC+H=C*COC*OOCCJ+H2    6.66E5 2.54 6.756E3
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011)degeneracy=2
C*COC*OOCC+H=C*COC*OOCJC+H2    1.2E6 2.4 2.583E3
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011)degeneracy=3
C*COC*OOCC+CH3=C*COC*OOCCJ+CH4    4.53E-1 3.65 7.154E3
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011)degeneracy=2
C*COC*OOCC+CH3=C*COC*OOCJC+CH4    1.2E-9 6.36 8.93E2
!Assume rate rule for primary from Sarathy et al, C8,C_F(2011)degeneracy=3
C*COC*OOCC+O=C*COC*OOCCJ+OH    9.81E5 2.43 4.75E3
!Assume rate rule for tertiary from Sarathy et al,C8,C_F(2011)degeneracy=2
C*COC*OOCC+O=C*COC*OOCJC+OH    7.66E5 2.41 1.14E3
!---------------------------------------
!***  Radical addition to c*coc*oocc ***
!---------------------------------------
!Analogy with ch2o+h=ch2oh, Held and Dryer, IJCK, 30,805 (1998)
C*COC*OOCC+H=>C*COC*OOH+C2H5    3.79E16 -1.39 5.402E3
!-------------------------------------------------
!***  consumption of radical from c*coc*oocc   ***
!-------------------------------------------------
!WJP: Reverse rate fit from ChemRev. Trange(K) = [ 300 -  5000] ; S= 4.3E-02
C*COC*OOCCJ=C2H4+CH2CHO+CO2    3.397E20 -2.6747 3.38143E4
!Analogy with reaction rate rule ch3ch2ch2c*o+ch2o=ch3ch2ch2c*oocj from Huynh and Violi JOC 2008.
C*COCJ*O+CH3CHO=C*COC*OOCJC    1.11E1 3.14 1.1198E4
!Analogy with rate of ch3+co2=ch3oco from Glaude 2003: CBSQ+isodesmic rxn+rotor calcs
C*COCJ*O=C2H3+CO2    2.33E11 0.55 1.362E4
! Assume barrier height is the same as ch3o+co=ch3oco from Glaude 2003 (about 9 kcal): CBSQ+isodesmic rxn+rotor calcs
C*COCJ*O=CH2CHO+CO    5.0E12 0.5 8.0E3
! Unlike ch3o+co=ch3oco, exothermic direction is in the decomposition direction.  Use A-factor similar to ch3oco=)ch3o+co.
!                                 ******************************************************************
!                                                  *** Low-temperature reactions ***
!                                 ******************************************************************
!---------------------
!*** Class 11 R+O2 ***
!---------------------
!primary ("-2" means -oo on primary site)
CJCOC*OOCC+O2=>CCOC*OOCCOO-2    4.52E12 0.0 0.0E0
! Reduce Ea by 2 kcal
CCOC*OOCCOO-2=>CJCOC*OOCC+O2    1.47E18 -1.199 3.421592E4
! ("-1" means -oo on secondry site)
!use tertiary rate since site is more like tertiary
CCJOC*OOCC+O2=>CCOC*OOCCOO-1    1.41E13 0.0 0.0E0
! Reduce Ea further by 2 kcal
CCOC*OOCCOO-1=>CCJOC*OOCC+O2    1.83E23 -2.19 3.21E4
!----------------------------
!*** Class 12 R+ROO=RO+RO ***
!----------------------------
!HN Sarathy et al. CF2011
CJCOC*OOCC+CCOC*OOCCOO-2=2CCOC*OOCCO-2    7.0E12 0.0 -1.0E3
!HN Sarathy et al. CF2011
CJCOC*OOCC+CCOC*OOCCOO-1=CCOC*OOCCO-2+CCOC*OOCCO-1    7.0E12 0.0 -1.0E3
!HN Sarathy et al. CF2011
CCJOC*OOCC+CCOC*OOCCOO-2=CCOC*OOCCO-1+CCOC*OOCCO-2    7.0E12 0.0 -1.0E3
!HN Sarathy et al. CF2011
CCJOC*OOCC+CCOC*OOCCOO-1=2CCOC*OOCCO-1    7.0E12 0.0 -1.0E3
!----------------------------
!*** Class 13 R+HO2=RO+OH ***
!----------------------------
!HN Sarathy et al. CF2011
CJCOC*OOCC+HO2=CCOC*OOCCO-2+OH    7.0E12 0.0 -1.0E3
!HN Sarathy et al. CF2011
CCJOC*OOCC+HO2=CCOC*OOCCO-1+OH    7.0E12 0.0 -1.0E3
!--------------------------------
!*** Class 14 R+CH3O2=RO+CH3O ***
!--------------------------------
!HN Sarathy et al. CF2011
CJCOC*OOCC+CH3O2=CCOC*OOCCO-2+CH3O    7.0E12 0.0 -1.0E3
!HN Sarathy et al. CF2011
CCJOC*OOCC+CH3O2=CCOC*OOCCO-1+CH3O    7.0E12 0.0 -1.0E3
!---------------------------------------
!*** Class 15 RO2=QOOH isomerization ***
!---------------------------------------
!CBS-QB3//MP2/6-311G(d,p) calculations, H. Nakamura 8-20-2012:
!5alpha, 5-membered alpha. CBS-QB3//MP2/6-311G(d,p)  H. Nakamura 7-28-2014
CCOC*OOCCOO-2=CCOC*OOCJCOOH-2    2.95E12 0.0 2.862E4
!9alpha, 9-membered alpha, CBS-QB3//MP2/6-311G(d,p), H. Nakamura 7-28-2014
CCOC*OOCCOO-2=CCJOC*OOCCOOH-2    2.31E11 0.0 2.137E4
!5-membered primary, CBS-QB3//MP2/6-311G(d,p), H. Nakamura 8-20-2012
CCOC*OOCCOO-1=CCOC*OOCCJOOH-1    5.86E11 0.0 3.376E4
!8-membered alpha, CBS-QB3//MP2/6-311G(d,p), H. Nakamura 8-20-2012
CCOC*OOCCOO-1=CCJOC*OOCCOOH-1    2.59E9 0.0 1.791E4
!9-membered primary, CBS-QB3//MP2/6-311G(d,p), H. Nakamura 8-20-2012
CCOC*OOCCOO-1=CJCOC*OOCCOOH-1    9.18E8 0.0 1.916E4
